ir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles }`\n     - `RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` - runs both binaries and compares\n     - `BuildBinary(t, \".\")` - compiles the cmd/ package\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that R5.1-R5.4 are about exit codes and error handling, which require testing error paths (unwritable output, nonexistent directories, etc.)\n   - The existing `runSponge` helper fatals on non-zero exit codes, so new test helpers or direct `exec.Command` usage will be needed for error-path tests that expect exit code 1\n   - The `DiffTest.ExitCode` field can be used to test expected non-zero exits via `RunDiffTests`\n   - R5.1 (exit 0) is implicitly covered by existing tests but should have explicit test cases\n   - R5.2 (exit 1 on errors) needs tests with: unwritable output path, nonexistent parent directory for output\n   - R5.3 (memory allocation) is hard to test directly in differential testing; may need to verify large inputs don't panic\n   - R5.4 (temp file cleanup) may need custom tests checking temp directory after sponge exits with error\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The massive task prompt containing the full project context, task description, constraints, execution constitution, required reading, requirements (R1-R4 mapping to srd007-sponge R5.1-R5.4), design decisions (D1: extend existing test file, D2: modify main.go if needed), and acceptance criteria (AC1-AC4)\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Add test cases to `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` covering R5.1 (exit 0 on success), R5.2 (exit 1 on errors with stderr messages), R5.3 (exit 1 on memory failures, no panic), R5.4 (temp file cleanup on error paths)\n   - Check if `main.go` needs any modifications for R5.x behavi